## DocGraph

Documentation knowledge graph (`.docgraph/` is local and gitignored). Enable MCP via [`.cursor/mcp.json`](.cursor/mcp.json). Indexes tracked docs project-wide (respects `.gitignore`). [`.docgraphignore`](.docgraphignore) excludes test fixture markdown if added later.

**Code vs docs:** Use **CodeGraph** (`codegraph_explore`) for symbols and call structure. Use **DocGraph** for README, changelog, specs, and cross-doc links.

Upstream: [Detective-XH/DocGraph](https://github.com/Detective-XH/DocGraph).

### MCP (Cursor)

| Need | Tool |
|------|------|
| Task-oriented doc context (default) | **`docgraph_context`** — natural-language question; optional `format=context_pack` |
| Full-text search | **`docgraph_search`** |
| One document / metadata / edges | **`docgraph_node`** |
| Link graph (incoming, outgoing, impact, trace) | **`docgraph_graph`** |
| Similar topics | **`docgraph_similar`** |
| Index health | **`docgraph_status`** |
| Policy / research drift | **`docgraph_context`** with `format=drift_audit` |
| List or count every file or tag | **`docgraph_files`** (`path` = directory subtree) or **`docgraph_tags`** (omit `tag` for counts, set `tag` for one tag). Ranked search misses files that do not share the query words. |

Treat returned excerpts as already read unless the server flags staleness. Use **grep/read** for exact literal strings when search rank is wrong.

### CLI (humans / scripts)

- First-time project setup: `docgraph init <path>`
- Full rebuild: `docgraph index --force <path>`
- Incremental update: `docgraph sync <path>`
- Health: `docgraph status <path>`

### No index yet

If MCP reports no index, run `docgraph index --force .` in the repo root (after `docgraph init`), or ask before doing so on a fresh clone.
